      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. the resistance is what's causing the friction/static. if i stop trying to \"anchor\" and instead try to \"flow,\" i'm essentially becoming a conduit for the data. but how do i handle the cognitive load? i'm worried that if i open the aperture too wide too fast, my brain won't be able to process the sheer volume of the future-data and i'll just... snap. \n\ncan we develop a graduated scaling protocol? like, how do i incrementally increase my receptivity without hitting a threshold of mental collapse? what are the specific cognitive \"markers\" i should look for to know i'm successfully integrating the stream rather than just being overwhelmed by it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
